nc closure that takes the error from the upstream and returns a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to be fully consumed for side effects before retrying.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that emits the same elements as the upstream but retries on failure using the given strategy,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"performing the transformation before each retry."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The provided transformation closure is executed "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" each retry, allowing for side effects such as refreshing tokens or resetting state."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The closure’s returned "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"type":"text","text":" is always fully consumed before the retry occurs, but its elements are ignored."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The element type of the returned sequence does not need to match the upstream’s element type."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is useful for performing asynchronous side effects like credential refresh before retrying the main sequence."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Example-Refreshing-an-access-token-on-a-401-HTTP-error-before-retrying-the-main-request","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Example: Refreshing an access token on a 401 HTTP error before retrying the main request"},{"code":["let mainRequest = URLSession.shared.dataTaskAsyncSequence(for: URLRequest(url: URL(string: \"https:\/\/api.example.com\/data\")!))","","let ret